  "raw": "en Español\n\n713 \nABNT20 KNHC 181726\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 PM EDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nEastern Subtropical Atlantic (AL99):\nShowers and thunderstorms have changed little in organization since \nthis morning in association with an area of low pressure located \nseveral hundred miles southwest of the Azores. However, just a small \nincrease in organization is likely to result in the formation of a \ntropical depression as soon as later today. The system is expected \nto move slowly over the next couple of days remaining southwest of \nthe Azores, followed by a turn to the southwest by early next week, \nwhen environmental conditions are forecast to become less favorable \nfor additional development. \n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...70 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...70 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Papin"
